<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Definitions and Standing Assumptions</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Probability measures.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of Borel probability measures on
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and a measurable function <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>,
we write <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mu}[g]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}g(\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mu}[g]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}g(\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> whenever the
integral is well-defined.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Kernel Regularity <span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K1</span>–<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K4</span>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a kernel satisfying:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K1.</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Characteristic.</span><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> 
The kernel </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is positive definite, and the mean embedding
</span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\mapsto\int k(\cdot,\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\mapsto\int k(\cdot,\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is injective on
</span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K2.</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Uniform gradient bound.</span><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> 
</span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{k}:=\sup_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\bigl\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\bigr\|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{k}:=\sup_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\bigl\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\bigr\|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K3.</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Strict positivity.</span><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> 
</span><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K4.</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Differentiability.</span><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> 
For every </span><math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the map
</span><math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\mapsto k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\mapsto k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is continuously differentiable.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Normalized KDE)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a translation-invariant kernel <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\varphi(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\varphi(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi\in L^{1}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi\in L^{1}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\|\varphi\|_{L^{1}}=:Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\|\varphi\|_{L^{1}}=:Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The normalized density <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}_{h}:=\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}/Z_{k}\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}_{h}:=\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}/Z_{k}\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfies <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log\bar{\mu}_{h}=\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log\bar{\mu}_{h}=\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so all
score-based formulas are unaffected by the normalization constant.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Injectivity of the KDE Operator</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show that a characteristic kernel allows the recovery of the
original measure from its KDE.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(KDE Injectivity)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="item K1. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K1.</span></a>. If <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\nu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\nu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\nu</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the RKHS of <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and denote the mean embeddings
<math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mu}:=\int k(\cdot,\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mu}:=\int k(\cdot,\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\nu}:=\int k(\cdot,\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\nu(\mathbf{y})\in\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\nu}:=\int k(\cdot,\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\nu(\mathbf{y})\in\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the reproducing property,
<math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mu}(\mathbf{x})=\langle m_{\mu},k(\cdot,\mathbf{x})\rangle_{\mathcal{H}_{k}}=\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mu}(\mathbf{x})=\langle m_{\mu},k(\cdot,\mathbf{x})\rangle_{\mathcal{H}_{k}}=\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>
and similarly for <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}=\nu_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}=\nu_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> pointwise
implies <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle m_{\mu}-m_{\nu},k(\cdot,\mathbf{x})\rangle_{\mathcal{H}_{k}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle m_{\mu}-m_{\nu},k(\cdot,\mathbf{x})\rangle_{\mathcal{H}_{k}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all
<math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{k(\cdot,\mathbf{x}):\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{k(\cdot,\mathbf{x}):\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\}</annotation></semantics></math> spans a dense subset
of <math id="A2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain <math id="A2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mu}=m_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mu}=m_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="item K1. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K1.</span></a> (injectivity of the mean embedding), <math id="A2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\nu</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We establish that the smoothness of <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> is inherited
entirely from the kernel, regardless of the regularity of <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(KDE Regularity)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <a href="#A1.I1.i2" title="item K2. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K2.</span></a>–<a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a> and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>
be arbitrary. Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}\in C^{1}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}\in C^{1}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and differentiation commutes with
integration:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\,\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\,\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\mathbf{x}}\|\nabla\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\|\leq M_{k}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\mathbf{x}}\|\nabla\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\|\leq M_{k}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.I1.i1" title="item (i) ‣ Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">: 
By <a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a>, <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\mapsto k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\mapsto k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <a href="#A1.I1.i2" title="item K2. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K2.</span></a>, <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\|\leq M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\|\leq M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for all
<math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the constant <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is trivially
<math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-integrable (<math id="A3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int M_{k}\mathrm{d}\mu=M_{k}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int M_{k}\mathrm{d}\mu=M_{k}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for any
probability measure <math id="A3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>), the Leibniz integral rule yields
(<a href="#A3.E10" title="In item (i) ‣ Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) and continuity of the derivative.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.I1.i2" title="item (ii) ‣ Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">: 
By <a href="#A1.I1.i3" title="item K3. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K3.</span></a>, <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is a nonzero positive measure,
<math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\int k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\int k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.I1.i3" title="item (iii) ‣ Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(iii)</span></a><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">: 
<math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\|=\bigl\|\int\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})\bigr\|\leq\int\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\|\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})\leq M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\|=\bigl\|\int\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})\bigr\|\leq\int\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\|\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})\leq M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, the KDE densities <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{kde}},q_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{kde}},q_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> are
strictly positive and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, the log-ratio
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(p_{\mathrm{kde}}/q_{\mathrm{kde}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(p_{\mathrm{kde}}/q_{\mathrm{kde}})</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence machinery of the next section applies to
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{kde}},q_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{kde}},q_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> with no additional assumptions on <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Wasserstein Gradient Flows of <math id="A4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-Divergences</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We recall the Wasserstein gradient flow (WGF)
framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ambrosio et al. [2005]</a></cite>
for <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergences between smooth positive densities.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:(0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:(0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be convex with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For positive densities <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho,\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho,\pi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{f}(\rho\|\pi):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\pi(\mathbf{x})\,f\!\left(\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\pi(\mathbf{x})}\right)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.427em;" width="0.427em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}(\rho\|\pi):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\pi(\mathbf{x})\,f\!\left(\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\pi(\mathbf{x})}\right)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(First Variation, Velocity, and Energy Dissipation)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho,\pi\in C^{1}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho,\pi\in C^{1}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho,\pi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho,\pi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> everywhere and
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{f}(\rho\|\pi)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}(\rho\|\pi)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The first variation of </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{f}(\rho\|\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}(\rho\|\pi)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with respect to
</span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is</span></p>
<table id="A4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\delta D_{f}(\rho\|\pi)}{\delta\rho}(\mathbf{x})=f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\pi(\mathbf{x})}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\delta D_{f}(\rho\|\pi)}{\delta\rho}(\mathbf{x})=f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\pi(\mathbf{x})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The WGF particle velocity is</span></p>
<table id="A4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{f}(\mathbf{x})=-\nabla f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\pi(\mathbf{x})}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{f}(\mathbf{x})=-\nabla f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\pi(\mathbf{x})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose in addition that the boundary terms arising
from integration by parts vanish:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lim_{R\to\infty}\int_{\|\mathbf{x}\|=R}\rho_{t}\,f^{\prime}\!\bigl(\tfrac{\rho_{t}}{\pi}\bigr)\,\nabla f^{\prime}\!\bigl(\tfrac{\rho_{t}}{\pi}\bigr)\cdot\hat{\mathbf{n}}\,dS=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{R\to\infty}\int_{\|\mathbf{x}\|=R}\rho_{t}\,f^{\prime}\!\bigl(\tfrac{\rho_{t}}{\pi}\bigr)\,\nabla f^{\prime}\!\bigl(\tfrac{\rho_{t}}{\pi}\bigr)\cdot\hat{\mathbf{n}}\,dS=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then along any smooth WGF solution </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}D_{f}(\rho_{t}\|\pi)=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\rho_{t}(\mathbf{x})\left\|\nabla f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{\rho_{t}(\mathbf{x})}{\pi(\mathbf{x})}\right)\right\|^{2}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}D_{f}(\rho_{t}\|\pi)=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\rho_{t}(\mathbf{x})\left\|\nabla f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{\rho_{t}(\mathbf{x})}{\pi(\mathbf{x})}\right)\right\|^{2}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(i)</em><span id="A4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text"> 
Let <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth, compactly-supported perturbation with
<math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\eta\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\eta\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:=\rho/\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:=\rho/\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left.\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\right|_{\epsilon=0}D_{f}(\rho+\epsilon\eta\|\pi)=\int\pi\,f^{\prime}(u)\,\frac{\eta}{\pi}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\int f^{\prime}(u)\,\eta\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>η</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left.\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\right|_{\epsilon=0}D_{f}(\rho+\epsilon\eta\|\pi)=\int\pi\,f^{\prime}(u)\,\frac{\eta}{\pi}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\int f^{\prime}(u)\,\eta\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">giving (<a href="#A4.E12" title="In item (i) ‣ Proposition D.2 (First Variation, Velocity, and Energy Dissipation). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii)</em><span id="A4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"> 
Immediate from Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition 3.4 (Wasserstein-2 gradient flow). ‣ 3.4 Wasserstein Gradient Flows ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>:
<math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{f}=-\nabla\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}}{\delta\rho}=-\nabla f^{\prime}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{f}=-\nabla\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}}{\delta\rho}=-\nabla f^{\prime}(u)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(iii)</em><span id="A4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> 
Write <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:=f^{\prime}(\rho_{t}/\pi)=\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}}{\delta\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:=f^{\prime}(\rho_{t}/\pi)=\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}}{\delta\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the continuity equation (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In Definition 3.4 (Wasserstein-2 gradient flow). ‣ 3.4 Wasserstein Gradient Flows ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}D_{f}(\rho_{t}\|\pi)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Phi\,\partial_{t}\rho_{t}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Phi\,\nabla\cdot\!\bigl(\rho_{t}\nabla\Phi\bigr)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em">∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.052em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}D_{f}(\rho_{t}\|\pi)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Phi\,\partial_{t}\rho_{t}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Phi\,\nabla\cdot\!\bigl(\rho_{t}\nabla\Phi\bigr)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The product rule gives
<math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi\,\nabla\cdot(\rho_{t}\nabla\Phi)=\nabla\cdot(\Phi\,\rho_{t}\nabla\Phi)-\rho_{t}\|\nabla\Phi\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em">∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\,\nabla\cdot(\rho_{t}\nabla\Phi)=\nabla\cdot(\Phi\,\rho_{t}\nabla\Phi)-\rho_{t}\|\nabla\Phi\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Integrating the divergence term over <math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying the
divergence theorem yields the boundary integral</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{\|\mathbf{x}\|=R}\rho_{t}\,\Phi\,(\nabla\Phi\cdot\hat{\mathbf{n}})\,dS," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\|\mathbf{x}\|=R}\rho_{t}\,\Phi\,(\nabla\Phi\cdot\hat{\mathbf{n}})\,dS,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">which vanishes as <math id="A4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>
by (<a href="#A4.E14" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proposition D.2 (First Variation, Velocity, and Energy Dissipation). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>). Hence</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}D_{f}(\rho_{t}\|\pi)=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\rho_{t}\|\nabla\Phi\|^{2}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}\leq 0.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}D_{f}(\rho_{t}\|\pi)=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\rho_{t}\|\nabla\Phi\|^{2}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}\leq 0.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Boundary condition (<a href="#A4.E14" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proposition D.2 (First Variation, Velocity, and Energy Dissipation). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>))<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We distinguish two settings and don’t assume the vanishing-boundary condition (<a href="#A4.E14" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proposition D.2 (First Variation, Velocity, and Energy Dissipation). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>). Within <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, in our context we assume the original <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and the induced KDE distributions can be easily satisfy the vanishing-boundary condition.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2em;">
<li id="A4.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="A4.I2.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Condition (</span><a href="#A4.E14" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proposition D.2 (First Variation, Velocity, and Energy Dissipation). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) is an assumption on the
joint tail behavior of </span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. It holds whenever
</span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, their ratio, and its gradient have sufficient
decay at infinity. In the context of this paper, </span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and
</span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are KDE-smoothed densities, whose tails are governed by
the kernel. For any kernel with exponential or faster decay
(e.g., Gaussian, Matérn with </span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, Pseudo-Huber), the
KDE-smoothed densities inherit exponential decay and the
condition is satisfied for all </span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with finite
second moments. For kernels with only polynomial decay
(e.g., IMQ with exponent </span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), the condition requires
</span><math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;(d-2)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;(d-2)/2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="A4.I2.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If the ambient space is a compact Riemannian manifold </span><math id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
without boundary,
then condition (</span><a href="#A4.E14" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proposition D.2 (First Variation, Velocity, and Energy Dissipation). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) is
</span><em id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph">vacuous</em><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Indeed, the divergence theorem on </span><math id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> reads</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{M}\nabla_{g}\cdot X\,d\mathrm{vol}_{g}=\int_{\partial M}g(X,\hat{\mathbf{n}})\,dS=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>vol</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{M}\nabla_{g}\cdot X\,d\mathrm{vol}_{g}=\int_{\partial M}g(X,\hat{\mathbf{n}})\,dS=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">since </span><math id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial M=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial M=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Consequently, the energy
dissipation inequality (</span><a href="#A4.E15" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proposition D.2 (First Variation, Velocity, and Energy Dissipation). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) holds
unconditionally for any </span><math id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-divergence, any
kernel satisfying the manifold analogues
of </span><a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="item K1. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K1.</span></a><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">–</span><a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and any </span><math id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in\mathcal{P}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in\mathcal{P}(M)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Identifiability for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence gradient flows)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a connected Riemannian manifold (e.g., <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> or
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>). Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho,\pi\in C^{1}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho,\pi\in C^{1}(M)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho,\pi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho,\pi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{M}\rho\,d\mathrm{vol}=\int_{M}\pi\,d\mathrm{vol}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>vol</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>vol</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{M}\rho\,d\mathrm{vol}=\int_{M}\pi\,d\mathrm{vol}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly convex and the WGF velocity vanishes
identically, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{f}\equiv\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{f}\equiv\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#A4.E13" title="In item (ii) ‣ Proposition D.2 (First Variation, Velocity, and Energy Dissipation). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{f}\equiv\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{f}\equiv\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> implies
<math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f^{\prime}(\rho/\pi)\equiv\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f^{\prime}(\rho/\pi)\equiv\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is connected and <math id="A4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(\rho/\pi)\in C^{0}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(\rho/\pi)\in C^{0}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have <math id="A4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(\rho/\pi)\equiv c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(\rho/\pi)\equiv c</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
Strict convexity of <math id="A4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly monotone,
so <math id="A4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho/\pi\equiv(f^{\prime})^{-1}(c)=:\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho/\pi\equiv(f^{\prime})^{-1}(c)=:\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Integrating: <math id="A4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\rho=\lambda\int\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\rho=\lambda\int\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A4.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A4.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark D.5</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Specific <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergences)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Writing <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:=\rho(\mathbf{x})/\pi(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:=\rho(\mathbf{x})/\pi(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, we record the velocities for
the divergences of primary interest:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(u)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Divergence</span></th>
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(u)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Velocity </span><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{f}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{f}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\log u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\log u</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(\rho\|\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(\rho\|\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\log u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\log u</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log\pi-\nabla\log\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log\pi-\nabla\log\rho</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log u</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\rho)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-1/u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1/u</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\pi}{\rho}(\nabla\log\pi-\nabla\log\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mi>ρ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\pi}{\rho}(\nabla\log\pi-\nabla\log\rho)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}(u-1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}(u-1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\chi^{2}(\rho\|\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(\rho\|\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<th id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u-1)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\rho}{\pi}(\nabla\log\pi-\nabla\log\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\rho}{\pi}(\nabla\log\pi-\nabla\log\rho)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>KDE Score Formula</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We express the score of <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> as an expectation under <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>,
establishing sample computability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(KDE Score)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <a href="#A1.I1.i2" title="item K2. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K2.</span></a>–<a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for all <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{\int\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}{\int k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{\int\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}{\int k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a><a href="#A3.I1.i1" title="item (i) ‣ Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a>
and <a href="#A3.I1.i2" title="item (ii) ‣ Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a>,
<math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}\in C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}\in C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}=\nabla\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}/\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}=\nabla\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}/\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting (<a href="#A3.E10" title="In item (i) ‣ Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) gives (<a href="#A5.E16" title="In Proposition E.1 (KDE Score). ‣ Appendix E KDE Score Formula ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gaussian Kernel Score)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\exp\!\bigl(-\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}/(2h^{2})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\exp\!\bigl(-\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}/(2h^{2})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{h^{2}}\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\mu,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbf{x}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{h^{2}}\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\mu,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbf{x}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mu,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]:=\int\mathbf{y}\,k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})\big/\int k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mu,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]:=\int\mathbf{y}\,k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})\big/\int k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the Gaussian kernel,
<math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\frac{\mathbf{y}-\mathbf{x}}{h^{2}}k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\frac{\mathbf{y}-\mathbf{x}}{h^{2}}k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting into (<a href="#A5.E16" title="In Proposition E.1 (KDE Score). ‣ Appendix E KDE Score Formula ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{\int\frac{\mathbf{y}-\mathbf{x}}{h^{2}}k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}{\int k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}=\frac{1}{h^{2}}\!\left(\!\frac{\int\mathbf{y}\,k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}{\int k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}-\mathbf{x}\!\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi>𝐱</mi></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{\int\frac{\mathbf{y}-\mathbf{x}}{h^{2}}k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}{\int k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}=\frac{1}{h^{2}}\!\left(\!\frac{\int\mathbf{y}\,k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}{\int k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}-\mathbf{x}\!\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Identifiability</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this section, <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:=p_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:=p_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}:=q_{0,\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>kde</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}:=q_{0,\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math>
denote the KDE-smoothed densities of the target distribution <math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>
and the initial generated distribution <math id="A6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
By Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, both are strictly positive and
<math id="A6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> under Assumptions <a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="item K1. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K1.</span></a>–<a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a>, with no regularity
conditions on <math id="A6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider the Wasserstein-2 gradient
flow of the <math id="A6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence <math id="A6.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}[\rho]=D_{f}(\rho\|\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}[\rho]=D_{f}(\rho\|\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>,
i.e., the continuity equation</p>
<table id="A6.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial_{t}\rho_{t}=\nabla\cdot\bigl(\rho_{t}\nabla\Phi_{t}\bigr),\qquad\Phi_{t}:=f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{\rho_{t}}{\pi}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}\rho_{t}=\nabla\cdot\bigl(\rho_{t}\nabla\Phi_{t}\bigr),\qquad\Phi_{t}:=f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{\rho_{t}}{\pi}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with initial condition <math id="A6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark F.1</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Density-level vs. particle-level flow)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Equation (<a href="#A6.E18" title="In Appendix F Identifiability ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) describes the evolution of a smooth
density <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in the Wasserstein-2 metric. In the practical
training algorithm <a href="#S4.SS8" title="4.8 Training Pipeline ‣ 4 Method: Gradient Flow Drifting ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>, one evolves a finite
collection of particles whose empirical distribution is <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and estimates the velocity using the KDE density
<math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t,\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>kde</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t,\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> from a mini-batch. The convergence theorems
below apply to the idealized density-level flow;
the particle system is viewed as a consistent approximation
that converges to this flow in the large-sample limit.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Proof of Identifiability (Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 4.7 (Unified identifiability (Proof in Appendix )). ‣ 4.3 Unified Identifiability ‣ 4 Method: Gradient Flow Drifting ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof proceeds in two steps.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Constant density ratio.</span> 
By definition, <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{f}^{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=-\nabla f^{\prime}\!\bigl(q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})/p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>kde</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{f}^{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=-\nabla f^{\prime}\!\bigl(q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})/p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The hypothesis <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{f}^{\mathrm{kde}}\equiv\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>kde</mi></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{f}^{\mathrm{kde}}\equiv\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
thus implies</p>
<table id="A6.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})}{p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})}\right)=\mathbf{0}\quad\text{for all }\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f^{\prime}\!\left(\frac{q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})}{p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})}\right)=\mathbf{0}\quad\text{for all }\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be the ambient space (<math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> or a connected Riemannian
manifold). By Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{kde}},q_{\mathrm{kde}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{kde}},q_{\mathrm{kde}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
so the ratio <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\mathbf{x}):=q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})/p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\mathbf{x}):=q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})/p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A6.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and strictly positive. By the composition rule,
<math id="A6.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:=f^{\prime}\circ u\in C^{1}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:=f^{\prime}\circ u\in C^{1}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is connected and <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\Phi\equiv\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\Phi\equiv\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A6.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant: <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(u(\mathbf{x}))=c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(u(\mathbf{x}))=c</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Strict convexity of <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly monotone, hence
injective. Therefore <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\mathbf{x})=(f^{\prime})^{-1}(c)=:\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\mathbf{x})=(f^{\prime})^{-1}(c)=:\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mathrm{kde}}=\lambda\,p_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mathrm{kde}}=\lambda\,p_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math>
everywhere.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: KDE matching implies distribution matching.</span> 
Integrating both sides over <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{M}q_{\mathrm{kde}}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\lambda\int_{M}p_{\mathrm{kde}}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{M}q_{\mathrm{kde}}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\lambda\int_{M}p_{\mathrm{kde}}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">For a translation-invariant kernel,
<math id="A6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int q_{\mathrm{kde}}=\int p_{\mathrm{kde}}=Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int q_{\mathrm{kde}}=\int p_{\mathrm{kde}}=Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>
(Remark <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Remark A.2 (Normalized KDE). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>); on a compact manifold the same
equality holds by symmetry. Hence <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A6.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mathrm{kde}}=p_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mathrm{kde}}=p_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the injectivity of the KDE
operator under characteristic kernels
(Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (KDE Injectivity). ‣ Appendix B Injectivity of the KDE Operator ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>), <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=p</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark F.2</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(MMD identifiability)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the MMD functional (Proposition <a href="#A8.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition H.2 (MMD Flow Velocity). ‣ Appendix H MMD Gradient Flow ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.2</span></a>),
<math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{MMD}}\equiv\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>MMD</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{MMD}}\equiv\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> implies
<math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla(p_{\mathrm{kde}}-q_{\mathrm{kde}})\equiv\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla(p_{\mathrm{kde}}-q_{\mathrm{kde}})\equiv\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By connectedness, <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{kde}}-q_{\mathrm{kde}}=c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{kde}}-q_{\mathrm{kde}}=c</annotation></semantics></math>. Integrating
gives <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{kde}}=q_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{kde}}=q_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (KDE Injectivity). ‣ Appendix B Injectivity of the KDE Operator ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> yields <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=q</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Core Equivalence: Drifting as KL Gradient Flow</h2>

<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem G.1</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Core Equivalence)<span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Gaussian kernel and
<math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the drifting
field (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.5 The Drifting Model ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A7.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\mathbf{V}_{p,q}(\mathbf{x})=h^{2}\bigl(\nabla\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-\nabla\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr)=h^{2}\,\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathbf{x})\big|_{\rho=q_{\mathrm{kde}},\;\pi=p_{\mathrm{kde}}},}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\mathbf{V}_{p,q}(\mathbf{x})=h^{2}\bigl(\nabla\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-\nabla\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr)=h^{2}\,\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathbf{x})\big|_{\rho=q_{\mathrm{kde}},\;\pi=p_{\mathrm{kde}}},}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{KL}}=\nabla\log\pi-\nabla\log\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{KL}}=\nabla\log\pi-\nabla\log\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is the WGF velocity
of the KL divergence <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\rho\|\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\rho\|\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>
(Remark <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem5" title="Remark D.5 (Specific 𝑓-divergences). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply Corollary <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary E.2 (Gaussian Kernel Score). ‣ Appendix E KDE Score Formula ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> to <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> respectively:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle h^{2}\nabla\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h^{2}\nabla\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbf{x}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbf{x},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle h^{2}\nabla\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h^{2}\nabla\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbf{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting, the <math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> terms cancel:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\bigl(\nabla\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-\nabla\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr)=\mathbb{E}_{p,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbb{E}_{q,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]=\mathbf{V}_{p,q}(\mathbf{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\bigl(\nabla\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-\nabla\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr)=\mathbb{E}_{p,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbb{E}_{q,k_{h}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]=\mathbf{V}_{p,q}(\mathbf{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">The identification with <math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> follows from
Remark <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem5" title="Remark D.5 (Specific 𝑓-divergences). ‣ Appendix D Wasserstein Gradient Flows of 𝑓-Divergences ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a> with <math id="A7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=q_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=q_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=p_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=p_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math>
(both smooth and positive by Corollary <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary C.2. ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>MMD Gradient Flow</h2>

<div id="A8.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition H.1</span></span><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Squared MMD)<span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a positive-definite kernel <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> with RKHS <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the squared MMD between <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A8.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MMD}_{k}^{2}(q,p):=\frac{1}{2}\|m_{q}-m_{p}\|_{\mathcal{H}_{k}}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>MMD</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MMD}_{k}^{2}(q,p):=\frac{1}{2}\|m_{q}-m_{p}\|_{\mathcal{H}_{k}}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mu}:=\int k(\cdot,\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mu}:=\int k(\cdot,\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> is the mean embedding.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition H.2</span></span><span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(MMD Flow Velocity)<span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="item K1. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K1.</span></a>–<a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a>. The WGF of
<math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}[q]:=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{MMD}_{k}^{2}(q,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>MMD</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}[q]:=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{MMD}_{k}^{2}(q,p)</annotation></semantics></math> has particle velocity</span></p>
<table id="A8.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{MMD}}(\mathbf{x})=\int\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}(p-q)(\mathbf{y})=\nabla\bigl(p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>MMD</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{MMD}}(\mathbf{x})=\int\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}(p-q)(\mathbf{y})=\nabla\bigl(p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Perturb <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\to(1-\epsilon)q+\epsilon\delta_{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\to(1-\epsilon)q+\epsilon\delta_{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{q_{\epsilon}}=m_{q}+\epsilon(k(\cdot,\mathbf{x})-m_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{q_{\epsilon}}=m_{q}+\epsilon(k(\cdot,\mathbf{x})-m_{q})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Expanding and differentiating at <math id="A8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}}{\delta q}(\mathbf{x})=\langle m_{q}-m_{p},\,k(\cdot,\mathbf{x})\rangle_{\mathcal{H}_{k}}=m_{q}(\mathbf{x})-m_{p}(\mathbf{x})=q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}}{\delta q}(\mathbf{x})=\langle m_{q}-m_{p},\,k(\cdot,\mathbf{x})\rangle_{\mathcal{H}_{k}}=m_{q}(\mathbf{x})-m_{p}(\mathbf{x})=q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">using the reproducing property. The velocity is
<math id="A8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{MMD}}=-\nabla\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}}{\delta q}=\nabla(p_{\mathrm{kde}}-q_{\mathrm{kde}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>MMD</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{MMD}}=-\nabla\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}}{\delta q}=\nabla(p_{\mathrm{kde}}-q_{\mathrm{kde}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a><a href="#A3.I1.i1" title="item (i) ‣ Theorem C.1 (KDE Regularity). ‣ Appendix C Regularity of KDE-Smoothed Densities ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a>,
differentiation under the integral gives the first equality
in (<a href="#A8.E25" title="In Proposition H.2 (MMD Flow Velocity). ‣ Appendix H MMD Gradient Flow ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Superposition of Gradient Flows</h2>

<div id="A9.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition I.1</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Superposition)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{1},\mathcal{F}_{2}:\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{1},\mathcal{F}_{2}:\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be functionals with
well-defined first variations.
For any <math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the mixed functional
<math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{mix}}:=\alpha\mathcal{F}_{1}+\beta\mathcal{F}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{mix}}:=\alpha\mathcal{F}_{1}+\beta\mathcal{F}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> has WGF velocity</span></p>
<table id="A9.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{mix}}(\mathbf{x})=\alpha\,\mathbf{v}_{1}(\mathbf{x})+\beta\,\mathbf{v}_{2}(\mathbf{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{mix}}(\mathbf{x})=\alpha\,\mathbf{v}_{1}(\mathbf{x})+\beta\,\mathbf{v}_{2}(\mathbf{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}=-\nabla\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}_{i}}{\delta\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}=-\nabla\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}_{i}}{\delta\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By linearity of the first variation and the gradient:</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{mix}}=-\nabla\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{mix}}}{\delta\rho}=-\nabla\!\left(\alpha\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}_{1}}{\delta\rho}+\beta\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}_{2}}{\delta\rho}\right)=\alpha\mathbf{v}_{1}+\beta\mathbf{v}_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>mix</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.663em;" width="0.663em"><mo>∇</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\mathrm{mix}}=-\nabla\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{mix}}}{\delta\rho}=-\nabla\!\left(\alpha\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}_{1}}{\delta\rho}+\beta\frac{\delta\mathcal{F}_{2}}{\delta\rho}\right)=\alpha\mathbf{v}_{1}+\beta\mathbf{v}_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Unified framework.</h5>

<div id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A9.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Unified framework. ‣ Appendix I Superposition of Gradient Flows ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> summarizes the KDE-based gradient flow
velocities, all sample-computable via the score
formula (<a href="#A5.E16" title="In Proposition E.1 (KDE Score). ‣ Appendix E KDE Score Formula ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A9.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Unified KDE-based gradient flow framework.
All velocities are expressed via <math id="A9.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{kde}},q_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{kde}},q_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> and are
sample-computable.</figcaption>
<table id="A9.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A9.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A9.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">Functional</th>
<th id="A9.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">WGF velocity <math id="A9.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A9.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">Model</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A9.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A9.T2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\bar{q}_{h}\|\bar{p}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\bar{q}_{h}\|\bar{p}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A9.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}-\nabla\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}-\nabla\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.T2.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="A9.T2.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Drifting</span> (<math id="A9.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="/h^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">/h^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A9.T2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\bar{p}_{h}\|\bar{q}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\bar{p}_{h}\|\bar{q}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A9.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla(p_{\mathrm{kde}}/q_{\mathrm{kde}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla(p_{\mathrm{kde}}/q_{\mathrm{kde}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.T2.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">-</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T2.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T2.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A9.T2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\chi^{2}(\bar{q}_{h}\|\bar{p}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(\bar{q}_{h}\|\bar{p}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.T2.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A9.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\nabla(q_{\mathrm{kde}}/p_{\mathrm{kde}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\nabla(q_{\mathrm{kde}}/p_{\mathrm{kde}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.T2.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">-</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T2.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T2.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A9.T2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MMD}_{k_{h}}^{2}(q,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>MMD</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MMD}_{k_{h}}^{2}(q,p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.T2.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><math id="A9.T2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla(p_{\mathrm{kde}}-q_{\mathrm{kde}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla(p_{\mathrm{kde}}-q_{\mathrm{kde}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.T2.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">MMD generators</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Analysis of Specific Kernel Families</h2>

<div id="A10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We verify Assumptions <a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="item K1. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K1.</span></a>–<a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a> for several kernel families.
For each kernel, we also compute the <em id="A10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">score weight</em>
<math id="A10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(r)</annotation></semantics></math> defined by
<math id="A10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=-w(r)(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=-w(r)(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="A10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r:=\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:=\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A10.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.1 </span>Euclidean Kernels</h3>

<section id="A10.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">J.1.1 </span>Gaussian (RBF) Kernel</h4>

<div id="A10.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition J.1</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Gaussian kernel
<math id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}):=\exp\!\bigl(-\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}/(2h^{2})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}):=\exp\!\bigl(-\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}/(2h^{2})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfies <a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="item K1. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K1.</span></a>–<a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a>. Its score weight is
<math id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(r)=1/h^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(r)=1/h^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (constant).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Gaussian kernel, one additionally obtains
<math id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}\in C^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}\in C^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> with every derivative uniformly
bounded for any <math id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="item K1. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K1.</span></a><span id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">: 
The Fourier transform
<math id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\varphi}(\bm{\omega})=(2\pi h^{2})^{d/2}\exp(-h^{2}\|\bm{\omega}\|^{2}/2)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\varphi}(\bm{\omega})=(2\pi h^{2})^{d/2}\exp(-h^{2}\|\bm{\omega}\|^{2}/2)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sriperumbudur et al. [2010, Theorem 9]</a></cite>, a
translation-invariant kernel with strictly positive Fourier
transform is characteristic.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.I1.i2" title="item K2. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K2.</span></a><span id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">: 
<math id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{h}\|=\frac{r}{h^{2}}e^{-r^{2}/(2h^{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{h}\|=\frac{r}{h^{2}}e^{-r^{2}/(2h^{2})}</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Maximizing over <math id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>:
the maximum occurs at <math id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=h</annotation></semantics></math>, giving
<math id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{k}=\frac{1}{h}e^{-1/2}=\frac{1}{h\sqrt{e}}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>e</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}=\frac{1}{h}e^{-1/2}=\frac{1}{h\sqrt{e}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.I1.i3" title="item K3. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K3.</span></a><span id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">:  <math id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\cdot)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\cdot)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a>:  <math id="A10.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{h}\in C^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{h}\in C^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">J.1.2 </span>Matérn-<math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> Kernel</h4>

<div id="A10.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition J.2</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Matérn kernel with smoothness <math id="A10.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and length scale
<math id="A10.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\nu,\ell}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\frac{2^{1-\nu}}{\Gamma(\nu)}\left(\frac{\sqrt{2\nu}\,r}{\ell}\right)^{\!\nu}K_{\nu}\!\left(\frac{\sqrt{2\nu}\,r}{\ell}\right),\qquad r:=\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>ν</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\nu,\ell}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\frac{2^{1-\nu}}{\Gamma(\nu)}\left(\frac{\sqrt{2\nu}\,r}{\ell}\right)^{\!\nu}K_{\nu}\!\left(\frac{\sqrt{2\nu}\,r}{\ell}\right),\qquad r:=\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A10.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> is the modified Bessel function of the second kind,
satisfies all four assumptions if and only if <math id="A10.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="item K1. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K1.</span></a><span id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">: 
The Fourier transform
<math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\varphi}(\bm{\omega})\propto(2\nu/\ell^{2}+\|\bm{\omega}\|^{2})^{-(\nu+d/2)}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\varphi}(\bm{\omega})\propto(2\nu/\ell^{2}+\|\bm{\omega}\|^{2})^{-(\nu+d/2)}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all
<math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\nu,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\nu,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is characteristic.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.I1.i3" title="item K3. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K3.</span></a><span id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">:  <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\nu,\ell}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\nu,\ell}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\nu}(z)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\nu}(z)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\nu,\ell}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\nu,\ell}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a><span id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">: 
The sample path regularity theory of Matérn processes shows that
<math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\nu,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\nu,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\lceil\nu\rceil-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\lceil\nu\rceil-1}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, a cusp at <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0</annotation></semantics></math> (Laplace-like) violates <a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a>.
When <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, at least <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> regularity is guaranteed.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.I1.i2" title="item K2. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K2.</span></a><span id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">: 
When <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{\nu,\ell}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{\nu,\ell}\|</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous
(by <a href="#A1.I1.i4" title="item K4. ‣ Assumption A.1 (Kernel Regularity K1–K4). ‣ Probability measures. ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Standing Assumptions ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K4.</span></a>) and decays exponentially as <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
bounded. When <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the gradient diverges at <math id="A10.SS1.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">J.1.3 </span>Summary of Euclidean Kernels</h4>

