<section id="A10.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.2 </span>Spherical Kernels</h3>

<div id="A10.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On the unit sphere
<math id="A10.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}^{d-1}:=\{\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\|\mathbf{x}\|=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}^{d-1}:=\{\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\|\mathbf{x}\|=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> with the round metric,
we adapt the kernel assumptions.</p>
</div>
<section id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adapted assumptions.</h5>

<div id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the Riemannian gradient on <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A10.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2em;">
<li id="A10.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A10.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K1<sub id="A10.I1.ix1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub></span>.</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A10.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is characteristic on
<math id="A10.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A10.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K2<sub id="A10.I1.ix2.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub></span>.</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A10.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\|\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><mi>𝕊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msub><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\|\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A10.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K3<sub id="A10.I1.ix3.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub></span>.</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A10.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all
<math id="A10.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A10.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K4<sub id="A10.I1.ix4.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub></span>.</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A10.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\mapsto k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\mapsto k(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A10.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>
on <math id="A10.I1.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">J.2.1 </span>von Mises–Fisher (vMF) Kernel</h4>

<div id="A10.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition J.3</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The vMF kernel <math id="A10.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}):=\exp(\kappa\,\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}):=\exp(\kappa\,\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A10.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <span id="A10.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K1<sub id="A10.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub></span>–<span id="A10.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K4<sub id="A10.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub></span>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K1<sub id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: 
The Mercer expansion
<math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\sum_{\ell=0}^{\infty}a_{\ell}(\kappa)\sum_{m}Y_{\ell}^{m}(\mathbf{x})\overline{Y_{\ell}^{m}(\mathbf{y})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\sum_{\ell=0}^{\infty}a_{\ell}(\kappa)\sum_{m}Y_{\ell}^{m}(\mathbf{x})\overline{Y_{\ell}^{m}(\mathbf{y})}</annotation></semantics></math>
has coefficients <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\ell}(\kappa)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\ell}(\kappa)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since all eigenvalues are positive,
<math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> is universal and hence characteristic.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K3<sub id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">:  <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\kappa\,\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\kappa\,\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
 </span>K4<sub id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1.3" class="ltx_sub">S</sub><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">:  <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\kappa}\in C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\kappa}\in C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K2<sub id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: 
The Riemannian gradient is
<math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{\kappa}=\kappa\,k_{\kappa}\,\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>𝕊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{\kappa}=\kappa\,k_{\kappa}\,\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{y})=\mathbf{y}-(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{y})=\mathbf{y}-(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\kappa}\leq e^{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>κ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\kappa}\leq e^{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{y})\|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{y})\|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{\kappa}\|\leq\kappa e^{\kappa}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><mi>𝕊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>κ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{\kappa}\|\leq\kappa e^{\kappa}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition J.4</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Spherical Core Equivalence)<span id="A10.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> be the vMF kernel.
Define <math id="A10.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x}):=\int_{\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x}):=\int_{\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="A10.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A10.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A10.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The spherical KDE score is</span></p>
<table id="A10.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\kappa\,\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}\!\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\mu,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\kappa\,\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}\!\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\mu,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A10.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The spherical drifting field
</span><math id="A10.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{p,q}^{\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{x}):=\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}\!\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{p,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbb{E}_{q,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝕊</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{p,q}^{\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{x}):=\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}\!\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{p,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbb{E}_{q,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A10.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A10.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{p,q}^{\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{\kappa}\bigl(\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝕊</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{p,q}^{\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{\kappa}\bigl(\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})-\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(i)</em><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> 
The ambient gradient of <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>
is <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\mathbf{y}\,k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\mathbf{y}\,k_{\kappa}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the ambient gradient of
<math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\int\mathbf{y}\,k_{\kappa}\mathrm{d}\mu/\int k_{\kappa}\mathrm{d}\mu=\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\int\mathbf{y}\,k_{\kappa}\mathrm{d}\mu/\int k_{\kappa}\mathrm{d}\mu=\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Riemannian gradient is its tangential projection,
giving (<a href="#A10.E27" title="In item (i) ‣ Proposition J.4 (Spherical Core Equivalence). ‣ J.2.1 von Mises–Fisher (vMF) Kernel ‣ J.2 Spherical Kernels ‣ Appendix J Analysis of Specific Kernel Families ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii)</em><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> 
By linearity of <math id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\kappa}\bigl(\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}-\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}\bigr)=\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}\!\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{p,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbb{E}_{q,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]\bigr)=\mathbf{V}_{p,q}^{\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝕊</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\kappa}\bigl(\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log p_{\mathrm{kde}}-\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log q_{\mathrm{kde}}\bigr)=\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}\!\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{p,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]-\mathbb{E}_{q,k_{\kappa}}[\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}]\bigr)=\mathbf{V}_{p,q}^{\mathbb{S}}(\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">J.2.2 </span>Spherical Logarithmic Kernel</h4>

<div id="A10.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition J.5</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{2+c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{2+c}</annotation></semantics></math>. The spherical logarithmic kernel defined by</span></p>
<table id="A10.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}):=-\log\bigl(\alpha(1-\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y}+c)\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}):=-\log\bigl(\alpha(1-\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y}+c)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies all spherical assumptions <span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K1<sub id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub></span>–<span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K4<sub id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub></span>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z:=\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z:=\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the argument of the logarithm be denoted as <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(z):=\alpha(1-z+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(z):=\alpha(1-z+c)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K3<sub id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (Strict positivity): 
We analyze the bounds of <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(z)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, the term <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-z+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-z+c</annotation></semantics></math> achieves its minimum at <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=1</annotation></semantics></math> (yielding <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>) and its maximum at <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=-1</annotation></semantics></math> (yielding <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2+c</annotation></semantics></math>). Therefore,</span></span></p>
<table id="A10.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\alpha\cdot c\leq g(z)\leq\alpha(2+c)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\alpha\cdot c\leq g(z)\leq\alpha(2+c).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the given condition <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{2+c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{2+c}</annotation></semantics></math>, we strictly have <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(z)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(z)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;g(z)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;g(z)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=-\log(g(z))&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=-\log(g(z))&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> everywhere.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K4<sub id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (Continuous differentiability): 
Since <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(z)\geq\alpha\cdot c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(z)\geq\alpha\cdot c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the argument of the logarithm is strictly bounded away from zero. The functions <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto-\log(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto-\log(t)</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>) are smooth (<math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>). Therefore, their composition <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{c,\alpha}\in C^{\infty}(\mathbb{S}^{d-1}\times\mathbb{S}^{d-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{c,\alpha}\in C^{\infty}(\mathbb{S}^{d-1}\times\mathbb{S}^{d-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, which trivially implies <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K2<sub id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (Uniform gradient bound): 
The ambient gradient of the kernel with respect to <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></span></p>
<table id="A10.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\frac{d}{dz}\bigl[-\log(\alpha(1-z+c))\bigr]\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})=\frac{1}{1-z+c}\mathbf{y}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\frac{d}{dz}\bigl[-\log(\alpha(1-z+c))\bigr]\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})=\frac{1}{1-z+c}\mathbf{y}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The Riemannian gradient is the projection onto the tangent space <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A10.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}(\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha})=\frac{1}{1-z+c}\bigl(\mathbf{y}-(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})\mathbf{x}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>𝕊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}(\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha})=\frac{1}{1-z+c}\bigl(\mathbf{y}-(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})\mathbf{x}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">We compute its norm. Since <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math> are unit vectors, <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{y}-z\mathbf{x}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}-2z(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})+z^{2}\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}=1-z^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{y}-z\mathbf{x}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}-2z(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})+z^{2}\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}=1-z^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus:</span></p>
<table id="A10.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\|=\frac{\sqrt{1-z^{2}}}{1-z+c}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><mi>𝕊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\|=\frac{\sqrt{1-z^{2}}}{1-z+c}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{1-z^{2}}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{1-z^{2}}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-z+c\geq c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-z+c\geq c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the uniform bound <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha}\|\leq\frac{1}{c}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><mi>𝕊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\mathbb{S},\mathbf{x}}k_{c,\alpha}\|\leq\frac{1}{c}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">K1<sub id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">S</sub><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (Characteristic): 
We expand the kernel into a Taylor series:</span></span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log\alpha-\log\bigl((1+c)-z\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log\alpha-\log\bigl((1+c)-z\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log\alpha-\log(1+c)-\log\left(1-\frac{z}{1+c}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log\alpha-\log(1+c)-\log\left(1-\frac{z}{1+c}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the Maclaurin series for <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log(1-x)=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{x^{n}}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log(1-x)=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{x^{n}}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (which converges absolutely since <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{z}{1+c}\right|\leq\frac{1}{1+c}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{z}{1+c}\right|\leq\frac{1}{1+c}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>), we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A10.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\underbrace{-\log\bigl(\alpha(1+c)\bigr)}_{a_{0}}+\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\underbrace{\frac{1}{n(1+c)^{n}}}_{a_{n}}(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munder><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\underbrace{-\log\bigl(\alpha(1+c)\bigr)}_{a_{0}}+\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\underbrace{\frac{1}{n(1+c)^{n}}}_{a_{n}}(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">From the user condition <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{2+c}&lt;\frac{1}{1+c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{2+c}&lt;\frac{1}{1+c}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(1+c)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(1+c)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, which strictly implies <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. For all <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we clearly have <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because the kernel <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{c,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{c,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as a power series <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}a_{n}(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}a_{n}(\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <em id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, Schoenberg’s theorem guarantees that it is strictly positive definite on <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for any dimension <math id="A10.SS2.SSS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, it is a universal (and therefore characteristic) kernel.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark J.6</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Spherical Score for Logarithmic Kernel)<span id="A10.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Following the same logic as Proposition <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition J.4 (Spherical Core Equivalence). ‣ J.2.1 von Mises–Fisher (vMF) Kernel ‣ J.2 Spherical Kernels ‣ Appendix J Analysis of Specific Kernel Families ‣ Gradient Flow Drifting: Generative Modeling via Wasserstein Gradient Flows of KDE-Approximated Divergences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.4</span></a>, the spherical KDE score for this logarithmic kernel can be explicitly derived. Define the pairwise weight function <math id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{c}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}):=\frac{1}{1-\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y}+c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{c}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}):=\frac{1}{1-\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{y}+c}</annotation></semantics></math>. The ambient gradient of <math id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int W_{c}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathbf{y}\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int W_{c}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathbf{y}\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the Riemannian score is:</span></p>
<table id="A10.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}\left(\frac{\int W_{c}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathbf{y}\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}{\int k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>kde</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕊</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbb{S}}\log\mu_{\mathrm{kde}}(\mathbf{x})=\Proj_{T_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbb{S}}\left(\frac{\int W_{c}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathbf{y}\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}{\int k_{c,\alpha}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\mathrm{d}\mu(\mathbf{y})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Unlike the vMF kernel, the weighting factor <math id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{c}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{c}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> here is polynomial (specifically, inversely proportional to distance squared, analogous to the Euclidean IMQ kernel), which typically produces heavier tails and better global mode coverage.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
